hey guys this is Vadim and welcome to  max tech so it's been 10 years since  Apple released the original MacBook Air  and it hasn't changed a single time  until now Apple's new 2018 MacBook Air  has been completely redesigned to look  more like their 12-inch MacBook and it  all looks great except for a few things  that are keeping me from buying it right  now people bought the original MacBook  for a few different reasons one it was  cheap it was thin it was light it had  lots of ports and had great battery life  now the biggest problem with the new  2018 MacBook Air is that it costs $200  more than it did before making it only  $100 cheaper than the 13-inch MacBook  Pro and the 12-inch MacBook now I agree  that the new MacBook Air is better than  the 12-inch MacBook in basically every  way except it's a little bit thicker and  it's a little bit heavier the 13-inch  MacBook Pro is better in a few ways  which I'll get into in just a bit now I  personally think that Apple really  should have priced this at a maximum of  1099 because $11.99 is way too expensive  and it's way too close to the other  devices on to the second problem there's  only two ports they're both Thunderbolt  three ports which is really nice but the  old MacBook Air had a ton of ports and  this one just has two ports and you're  gonna need adapters for all your legacy  devices so that is a major issue for all  the casual users of course Thunderbolt 3  is nice because you can hook up really  fast drives you can hook up a 5k  external display and a bunch of other  stuff but the market that the MacBook  Air is targeted to doesn't really need  this stuff at all and the people who do  need those ports are just gonna go with  the 13-inch MacBook Pro anyways or maybe  even the 2018 MacBook Pro that starts at  $17.99 that's personally what I would  choose so overall a lot of the regular  consumers are gonna have big issues with  the two u.s. PC ports now onto the third  problem the MacBook Air is still packin  a dual-core processor while the rest of  the market is moving to four cores  I'm really not sure why Apple's stuck  with the dual core now I know that it  helps with battery life but it would  have been really nice to have that extra  upgrade option to a quad-core yes it  matches the 13-inch MacBook Pros turbo  boost of 3.6 gigahertz but the core  clock speed is a lot slower and it's a 7  watt chip instead of a 15 watt chip so  it's gonna draw a lot less power and  it's ultimately going to be slower not  only that but the new MacBook Airs  Fix performance is much worse than the  13-inch MacBook Pros in fact the MacBook  Pro gets 50 percent faster graphics  performance now of course that's why  it's called the MacBook Pro but if you  check B&amp;H it's only fifty dollars more  than the new MacBook Air for all the  extra power sure the target market  doesn't really need the extra power but  for me personally that's the only reason  why I haven't already ordered the  MacBook Air now onto the fourth reason  even though the new MacBook Air has a  Retina display it's actually worse than  the 13-inch MacBook Pros Retina display  the pro gets a brighter 500 nits display  which really helps we're using it  outside in the daylight or even in a  really bright room the pro also gets P  three wide color gamut support so it's  got much better color accuracy compared  to the air this is yet another reason to  choose the pro over the air for just $50  more for the fifth and final problem the  new MacBook Air is still using Bluetooth  4.2 basically every single 2018 Apple  device except for the budget iPad has  now moved on to Bluetooth 5 including  all the new iPhones the home pod the  Apple TV 4k the Mac Mini the MacBook  Pros and the new iPad pro since  everything else is moving on to  Bluetooth 5 it really sucks that Apple  chose to keep the macbook air at  bluetooth 4.2 of course it's not that  big of a deal yet because there isn't  that mini bluetooth 5 devices out there  but it's still a big deal to me so there  you have it guys that's the top 5  problems with the new MacBook Air thanks  for watching this video guys make sure  to leave a comment below and subscribe  for more videos like this one
 

